            <ArticleTitle>Steal phenomenon caused by a parallel branch of the internal mammary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>463-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a patient with postoperative mammary artery steal resulting from a parallel branch of the vessel as well as from a patent first left intercostal artery, both of which had not been divided. The patient was cured of angina pectoris after embolization of both vessels.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
